  "name": {
    "en": "A4 Maritsa Motorway"
  },
  "description": {
    "en": "The Maritsa motorway (A4) is a 117 km route in southern Bulgaria connecting the Trakia motorway (A1) near Chirpan to the Turkish border at Kapitan Andreevo. It is part of Pan-European Corridor IV and European route E80. The motorway was completed in phases between October 2010 and October 2015, with EU co-funding for the western sections (Chirpan–Haskovo, Haskovo–Harmanli) and national financing for the eastern sections."
  },
